@@ -0,0 +1,135 @@
+# RSpec Test Suite Profiling & Optimization Guide
+
+## 1. Baseline Metrics
+
+### `spec/models` (Baseline)
+- **Examples**: 1,795 examples (0 failures) across 152 files
+- **Wall Time**: **154.5 seconds (2 minutes 34.5 seconds)** (files took ~2.6s to load)
+- **Total Example Time**: 157.53s
+- **SQL Queries (`sql.active_record`)**: 113,959 queries (20.90s in DB execution)
+- **Factory Calls (`FPROF=1`)**: 4,721 total (3,243 top-level), 141.35s total time:
+  - `status`: 1,003 total (923 top-level) – 74.94s (0.0747s/call)
+  - `bookmark`: 1,019 total (17 top-level) – 38.86s (0.0381s/call)
+  - `account`: 1,194 total (1,136 top-level) – 35.06s (0.0294s/call)
+  - `media_attachment`: 40 total – 7.82s (0.1955s/call)
+  - `notification`: 76 total – 6.32s (0.0832s/call)
+  - `user`: 93 total (84 top-level) – 4.31s (0.0464s/call)
+  - `report`: 37 total – 2.43s (0.0657s/call)
+  - `custom_emoji`: 44 total – 1.54s (0.0351s/call)
+  - `admin_user`: 33 total – 1.27s (0.0384s/call)
+  - `login_activity`: 270 total (0 top-level) – 1.18s (0.0044s/call)
+
+#### Top 15 Slowest `spec/models` Files at Baseline
+1. `spec/models/account_statuses_cleanup_policy_spec.rb` – 16.12s (36 examples)
+2. `spec/models/tag_feed_spec.rb` – 12.78s (33 examples)
+3. `spec/models/status_spec.rb` – 12.19s (62 examples)
+4. `spec/models/trends/statuses_spec.rb` – 12.16s (12 examples)
+5. `spec/models/public_feed_spec.rb` – 8.92s (43 examples)
+6. `spec/models/notification_spec.rb` – 7.59s (25 examples)
+7. `spec/models/media_attachment_spec.rb` – 6.56s (27 examples)
+8. `spec/models/concerns/status/threading_concern_spec.rb` – 6.43s (16 examples)
+9. `spec/models/account_spec.rb` – 6.13s (122 examples)
+10. `spec/models/concerns/account/interactions_spec.rb` – 5.71s (71 examples)
+11. `spec/models/concerns/status/fetch_replies_concern_spec.rb` – 4.58s (15 examples)
+12. `spec/models/form/import_spec.rb` – 3.59s (93 examples)
+13. `spec/models/user_spec.rb` – 3.01s (73 examples)
+14. `spec/models/report_spec.rb` – 2.41s (17 examples)
+15. `spec/models/admin/moderation_action_spec.rb` – 2.25s (5 examples)
+
+---
+
+## 2. Phase 1 Root Causes & Optimizations Applied (`spec/models` + Global Config)
+
+1. **Global `ActiveRecord.verbose_query_logs = true` Leak**:
+   - `spec/models/concerns/status/fetch_replies_concern_spec.rb:6` set `ActiveRecord.verbose_query_logs = true` at the class-definition level of `RSpec.describe`.
+   - Because RSpec loads all spec files before running examples, this enabled `verbose_query_logs` globally across the entire run. Every SQL query walked the call stack (`Thread.each_caller_location`) and ran `Rails::BacktraceCleaner#clean_frame`, consuming **41.0% of total wall time (~65s)** and writing ~92 MB of logs per run to `log/test.log`.
+   - **Fix**: Removed `ActiveRecord.verbose_query_logs = true` from `spec/models/concerns/status/fetch_replies_concern_spec.rb` and set `config.log_level = ENV.fetch('RAILS_LOG_LEVEL', 'warn')` in `config/environments/test.rb`.
+
+2. **Global `Sidekiq.testing!(:inline)` & Unnecessary `TriggerWebhookWorker` / Mailer Execution**:
+   - `spec/rails_helper.rb` ran `Sidekiq.testing!(:inline)` before every example.
+   - Every `User`, local `Status`, `Account`, and `Report` creation/update triggers `TriggerWebhookWorker.perform_async(...)` in `after_create_commit` / `after_update_commit`.
+   - `WebhookService#call` serializes the entire object graph via `REST::Admin::WebhookEventSerializer` *before* checking if any `Webhook` records exist in the database. This accounted for **~23–26% of total wall time (~36.5s)** and ~43,000 extra SQL queries in `spec/models`.
+   - Furthermore, `config.active_job.queue_adapter = :sidekiq` combined with `Sidekiq.testing!(:inline)` caused `ActionMailer::MailDeliveryJob` to render HAML/Premailer emails on every unconfirmed `User` creation.
+   - **Fix**:
+     - Set `config.active_job.queue_adapter = :test` in `config/environments/test.rb` so emails are only rendered on demand inside `capture_emails` blocks.
+     - Changed `spec/rails_helper.rb` to use `Sidekiq.testing!(:fake)` by default for `type: :model` (with `:inline_workers` tag opt-in).
+
+3. **Paperclip Post-Processing Overhead (`spec/support/paperclip.rb`)**:
+   - Creating `MediaAttachment`, `CustomEmoji`, `Account` (avatar/header) ran `Vips`, `FFmpeg`, `ImageExtractor`, and `Blurhash` processors even in specs that only test database queries, associations, or validations.
+   - **Fix**: Added `PaperclipTestOptimization` in `spec/support/paperclip.rb` to skip `post_process_styles`, `flush_writes`, and `MediaAttachment#check_video_dimensions` in model specs unless tagged with `:paperclip_processing` (while keeping `check_validity?` active so content-type, size, filename obfuscation, and `set_type_and_extension` callbacks still run). Tagged media-processing examples in `spec/models/media_attachment_spec.rb` with `:paperclip_processing`.
+
+4. **Devise BCrypt Digest Memoization (`spec/rails_helper.rb`)**:
+   - `BCrypt::Engine.__bc_crypt` consumed ~3.0s (5.1% of remaining wall time) hashing the default test password `'123456789'` thousands of times.
+   - **Fix**: Memoized `Devise::Encryptor.digest` by `[klass.pepper, klass.stretches, password]` in `spec/rails_helper.rb`.
+
+5. **Redis Cleanup (`spec/rails_helper.rb`)**:
+   - Replaced `redis.del(redis.keys)` (2 Redis commands per example) with `redis.flushdb` (1 command).
+
+6. **Shared Setup Restructuring (`let_it_be` / `before_all`)**:
+   - Enabled `test_prof/recipes/rspec/let_it_be` with `default_modifiers[:reload] = true` in `spec/rails_helper.rb`.
+   - Converted repetitive `let!` / `before` database setups to `let_it_be` / `before_all` in the slowest model specs (`account_statuses_cleanup_policy_spec.rb`, `trends/statuses_spec.rb`, `tag_feed_spec.rb`, `public_feed_spec.rb`, `notification_spec.rb`, `status_spec.rb`, `concerns/status/threading_concern_spec.rb`, `concerns/status/fetch_replies_concern_spec.rb`, `concerns/account/interactions_spec.rb`, `form/import_spec.rb`, `account/search_spec.rb`, `concerns/account/finder_concern_spec.rb`, `account_suggestions/friends_of_friends_source_spec.rb`, `custom_emoji_filter_spec.rb`, `form/custom_emoji_batch_spec.rb`, `announcement_spec.rb`, `web/push_subscription_spec.rb`, `status_pin_spec.rb`, `collection_spec.rb`, `admin/moderation_action_spec.rb`, `admin/account_action_spec.rb`, `account_conversation_spec.rb`, `trends/links_spec.rb`).
+
+### `spec/models` Results After Phase 1
+- **Wall Time**: **~28.4 seconds** (down from **154.5 seconds** — **81.6% faster / 5.4x speedup**)
+- **Examples**: 1,795 examples, 0 failures
+
+---
+
+## 3. Insights & Plan for Future Optimization Phases
+
+### Phase 2: `spec/requests` (1,895 examples across 263 files)
+1. **Enable `Sidekiq.testing!(:fake)` for `type: :request`**:
+   - Out of all 263 files in `spec/requests`, **only 6 files** rely on `Sidekiq.testing!(:inline)`:
+     1. `spec/requests/api/v2/notifications/accounts_spec.rb`
+     2. `spec/requests/api/v1/statuses/favourites_spec.rb`
+     3. `spec/requests/api/v1/timelines/home_spec.rb`
+     4. `spec/requests/api/v1/notifications_spec.rb`
+     5. `spec/requests/api/v2/notifications_spec.rb`
+     6. `spec/requests/api/v1/conversations_spec.rb`
+   - Tagging those 6 files with `:inline_workers` allows switching `type: :request` to `Sidekiq.testing!(:fake)` by default (eliminating `TriggerWebhookWorker` and other background workers across the other 257 request spec files).
+   - Also stub `TriggerWebhookWorker.perform_async` when `:inline_workers` is used unless testing webhooks.
+
+2. **Route Reloading Bottleneck (`Rails.application.reload_routes!`)**:
+   - `spec/requests/signature_verification_spec.rb:13` (30 examples, ~8.95s) has `after { Rails.application.reload_routes! }` at the top level of `RSpec.describe`, reloading the entire Rails routing table 30 times, even though only **1 example** (around line 771) calls `Rails.application.routes.draw`! Moving `after { Rails.application.reload_routes! }` into that single context will save ~7–8 seconds.
+   - Check `spec/requests/api/v1/csp_spec.rb:8` for the same pattern.
+
+3. **Enable `PaperclipTestOptimization` for `type: :request`**:
+   - Extend `PaperclipTestOptimization` to `type: :request` and tag only the specific media upload request specs (`spec/requests/api/v1/media_spec.rb`, `spec/requests/api/v2/media_spec.rb`, `spec/requests/media_spec.rb`, etc.) that assert on processed media metadata with `:paperclip_processing`.
+
+4. **Shared Setup in Top Slowest `spec/requests` Files**:
+   - Top slowest `spec/requests` files (with `log_level = :warn` and `Sidekiq.testing!(:fake)`):
+     1. `spec/requests/cache_spec.rb` – 19.25s (258 examples)
+     2. `spec/requests/signature_verification_spec.rb` – 8.95s (30 examples)
+     3. `spec/requests/activitypub/replies_spec.rb` – 8.21s (45 examples)
+     4. `spec/requests/api/v1/timelines/public_spec.rb` – 2.28s (12 examples)
+     5. `spec/requests/api/v2/notifications_spec.rb` – 1.96s (29 examples)
+     6. `spec/requests/api/v1/profiles_spec.rb` – 1.73s (8 examples)
+     7. `spec/requests/activitypub/contexts_spec.rb` – 1.72s (7 examples)
+     8. `spec/requests/api/v1/media_spec.rb` – 1.71s (18 examples)
+     9. `spec/requests/api/v1/statuses_spec.rb` – 1.70s (36 examples)
+     10. `spec/requests/api/v1/timelines/link_spec.rb` – 1.68s (11 examples)
+   - Use `let_it_be` / `before_all` in `spec/requests/cache_spec.rb`, `spec/requests/activitypub/replies_spec.rb`, and `spec/support/api_authentication.rb` (`with API authentication` shared context).
+
+### Phase 3: Factories (`spec/fabricators/`)
+1. **`spec/fabricators/status_fabricator.rb:11-13`**:
+   ```ruby
+   after_create do |status|
+     Fabricate(:bookmark, status: status)
+   end
+   ```
+   - Every `Fabricate(:status)` unconditionally creates a `Bookmark`, which in turn builds and persists a new `Account` and `User` (and 2 `LoginActivity` records)!
+   - In `spec/models` alone, **1,002 out of 1,019 bookmarks** were created by this `after_create` hook on `:status` and never used. Removing this `after_create` hook will cut database inserts during status fabrication by more than half.
+
+2. **`spec/fabricators/user_fabricator.rb:16-18`**:
+   ```ruby
+   after_create do |user|
+     2.times { Fabricate(:login_activity, user: user) }
+   end
+   ```
+   - Every `Fabricate(:user)` unconditionally creates 2 `LoginActivity` records (270 unused `LoginActivity` inserts in `spec/models`). Removing this hook avoids 2 extra `INSERT` queries per user.
+
+3. **`spec/fabricators/account_fabricator.rb:13`**:
+   ```ruby
+   user { |attrs| attrs[:domain].nil? ? Fabricate.build(:user, account: nil) : nil }
+   ```
+   - Every local `Account` fabricates a `User` (even though `Account` does not require a `User` in the database or model validations).
